{"id": "EUVD-2026-82107", "enisaUuid": "472f6506-24f7-310b-b27d-b22dee4aa271", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nbpf: Fix CFI mismatch in task work callback\n\nBPF subprograms use the bpf_callback_t ABI, but task work invokes the\ncallback through a three-argument function pointer. This trips kCFI.\n\nStore and invoke the callback as bpf_callback_t.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:10:01", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:03:52", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/85a33c910edc3651f68b17ae3c597c012545958f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a2cbab47f44e9ea8c5a161ecba1b6bb8535771eb", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2805abd089576799b15092949420e3f8ba97fabd"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-92486", "GHSA-vh7j-gj65-xh7c"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1c135e68-48fb-3bc8-80c7-a2b637cc16a6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "38aa7003e369802f81a078f6673d10d97013f04f <a2cbab47f44e9ea8c5a161ecba1b6bb8535771eb"}, {"id": "365c0a36-e5aa-32b2-9dcd-5ffba91ef7f4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "403b6826-6e2f-3d20-ad44-248d6aa29952", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "38aa7003e369802f81a078f6673d10d97013f04f <2805abd089576799b15092949420e3f8ba97fabd"}, {"id": "7d281ea5-e5fc-3c5c-9869-40955b559010", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "94adc2ae-2948-3599-ad2e-c476972c8138", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.18"}, {"id": "a1d10e0e-d55d-33c1-9e3a-263021fb2a94", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.52"}, {"id": "e87f0513-8884-3132-80d1-fd330745215d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "38aa7003e369802f81a078f6673d10d97013f04